  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The plural and «un, una»",
   "texto": [
    "In Italian **no hay plural en -s**. As a general pattern, the **-o** names make the plural in **-i** (book → libri), those that end in **-a**, in **-e** (house → case), and those that end in **-e**, in **-i** (chiave → chiavi). There are irregular plurals and invariable names that you will learn little by little.",
    "The undefined article: **un** book, **uno** zaino (also before **s + consonante**), **un amico** (without apostrophe, masculine), **una** house, **un'amica** (with apótrophe, feminine).",
    "**Che cos'è?** = what is this? **È un libro** or, in plural, **Sono libri** is answered."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The colors",
   "texto": [
    "They go behind the name and match: **una borsa nera**, **i libri rossi**.",
    "**Verde** has a single form for masculine and feminine. **Blu** never changes."
   ]
  },
